[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Backend requirements
OPTIONS:
  VIEW_STYLE: Table

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @requirement

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Requirements for the FastAPI backend and web admin in ``backend/``, split into one document per feature. This index includes all feature documents, so the export shows them as one document with a chapter per feature. Verifications live in ``docs/verifications/backend/`` with the same file names.

.. list-table::
   :header-rows: 1

   * - Feature
     - File
     - UIDs
   * - Dashboard API
     - ``dashboard_api.sdoc``
     - REQ-BE-001 .. 009
   * - Setup and authentication
     - ``setup_auth.sdoc``
     - REQ-BE-010 .. 019
   * - People and permissions
     - ``people_permissions.sdoc``
     - REQ-BE-020 .. 029
   * - Tasks
     - ``tasks.sdoc``
     - REQ-BE-030 .. 039
   * - Agenda
     - ``agenda.sdoc``
     - REQ-BE-040 .. 049, REQ-BE-051
   * - Wall tablet upgrades
     - ``wall_tablet_upgrades.sdoc``
     - REQ-BE-050, 052 .. 059
   * - Afvalwijzer (optional)
     - ``afvalwijzer.sdoc``
     - REQ-BE-060 .. 069
   * - AI integration
     - ``ai_integration.sdoc``
     - REQ-BE-080 .. 089
   * - AI monitoring
     - ``ai_monitoring.sdoc``
     - REQ-BE-090 .. 099
   * - General
     - ``general.sdoc``
     - REQ-BE-070 .. 079

UIDs are permanent: a requirement keeps its UID when it moves. Each feature has a block of ten numbers; when a block is full, take the next free number and keep the requirement in its feature document (e.g. REQ-BE-051 belongs to Agenda). A feature-level requirement can be the ``Parent`` of the detailed requirements below it.
<<<

